{"reference":"Genesis 11","book":"Genesis","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading Genesis 1–11","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Genesis 1–11 belongs to an ancient Near Eastern literary environment in which creation, flood, genealogy, and city-building traditions were discussed. The chapter should be read as ancient theological and literary discourse; compositional models and Mosaic-attribution questions remain distinct positions because Genesis does not narrate its own literary formation.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_011_ab123309f8af48ee61b5f137"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
